{"id":"chatcmpl-39b22602-74d1-486f-b97e-76423f9f60ed","object":"chat.completion","created":1795248299,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"```json\n{\n  \"highlights\": \"This task demonstrates a conflict-resolution strategy for visual medical QA where multiple models disagree on spatial laterality. The key insight is to treat model disagreement as a signal to invoke an explicit verification step using orientation markers and anatomical landmarks rather than trusting either model blindly. The pattern generalizes to any task requiring side/location disambiguation in images.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"When multiple independent visual analysis tools disagree on a spatial attribute (side, location), escalate to an explicit verification step rather than defaulting to either output.\",\n    \"For laterality questions in medical images, always ground the answer in orientation markers (e.g., 'L' marker) and anatomical landmarks, not raw model output.\",\n    \"Use a second independent model as corroboration when the first model's spatial claim is uncertain or when the task hinges on a single ambiguous attribute.\",\n    \"Treat conflicting model outputs as a risk flag that must be resolved with targeted evidence before committing to a final answer.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Medical image QA\": \"Route laterality/location questions through at least two independent visual tools; if they conflict, run a verification step keyed to orientation markers and anatomy.\",\n    \"Multi-model consensus tasks\": \"When models disagree, don't average or pick arbitrarily—invoke a verification tool with a specific, falsifiable question about the disputed attribute.\",\n    \"Spatial disambiguation\": \"Anchor side/location answers to explicit image metadata (markers, labels) and cross-check against anatomical context before finalizing.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Confirm orientation markers (e.g., 'L'/'R' labels) and anatomical landmarks before assigning patient-side laterality.\",\n    \"If two visual tools disagree on the key attribute, run a dedicated verification step and document the resolution rationale.\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":562,"total_tokens":942,"completion_tokens":380,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":562},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":380}}}